pseudo-Boolean proof version 2.0
* Regression test (wrong verdict): defect 19's payload reached through the
* placement hole of incorrect/version2/order_definition_sol rather than
* through a set-membership one.
*
* `strengthening_to_core on` promises that the derived set holds nothing but
* constraints entailed by the core set, and it keeps that promise by moving
* the whole database to core. Executed inside the order definition it moved
* the EMPTY sub-database instead, while setting `context.is_strengthening_to_core`
* -- which is global, and survives the `end`. The outer derived set, which by
* then holds the merely satisfiability-preserving `1 y1 >= 1`, was never moved,
* so the following `red` was handed `add_derived_goals = false` and never had
* to preserve it. Two contradictory witnessed constraints then coexist and
* `u >= 1` closes the proof.
*
* `1 x1 1 x2 >= 1` is satisfied by `x1 = 1, x2 = 0`; the same binary verifies
* that in correct/version2/order_definition_strengthening_to_core_outside,
* whose proof is this one with the mode switch moved back to the top level,
* where it is correctly refused as an unproven proofgoal.
f 1
red 1 y1 >= 1 ; y1 -> 1 ;
pre_order simple
    strengthening_to_core on
    vars
        left u1
        right v1
        aux
    end
    def
        -1 u1 1 v1 >= 0 ;
    end
    transitivity
        vars
            fresh_right w1
        end
        proof
            proofgoal #1
                p -2 -3 + -1 +
            end -1
        end
    end
end
red 1 ~y1 >= 1 ; y1 -> 0 ;
u >= 1 ;
output NONE
conclusion UNSAT : -1
end pseudo-Boolean proof
